    "selector": "/variants/hack2hire:6a4d6a5560d5cca82da2fe23/variantLabel"
   }
  ]
 },
 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "Concurrency is modelled as a deterministic single-threaded call sequence. MutexTaskLock() starts idle with an empty FIFO wait queue. acquire(jobId, jobType) admits the job at once and returns true when the wait queue is empty and no job of the other type is running; otherwise it appends the job to the wait queue and returns false (the job is blocked). release(jobId) ends a running job; if no job is running afterwards, the longest prefix of the wait queue whose jobs share the type of its first job is admitted. release returns the ids admitted by that call in queue order (possibly empty). Every method call is answered in call order on one instance; void methods return nothing.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk17-a-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
    "sha256": "b379953144287fffb14d286c61502eb70825b215ff72daf1b6bde6281724ef8b",
    "selector": "/problems/16/inferred_spec"
   }
  ]
 },
